		)
	)
	(gr_text "ROUTING GUIDE\nBottom layer: one GND pour over the whole board. Every GND pad lands in it.\nTop layer, wide pours (net class Tank, 0.8 mm gap):\n  DRAIN_Q2 = Net-(D3-C): J2-1, C1-1, C2-1, D3-C, Q2-D  (west column)\n  DRAIN_Q1 = Net-(D4-C): J2-3, C1-2, C2-2, D4-C, Q1-D  (east column)\n  Each column passes under R1/R2 or between the gate parts and the edge.\nTop layer, power (net class Power, 3 mm):\n  VIN: J1-1 to F1-1.   VCC: F1-2, C4-1, C3-1, L1-1, R1-1, R2-2.\nTop layer, 0.5 mm signal:\n  GATE_Q2 = Net-(D2-K): Q2-G north under R2 and D3, then R4-1, D2-K, R1-2, D4-A.\n  GATE_Q1 = Net-(D1-K): D3-A, D1-K, R2-1, R3-2.\nBottom layer links (no vias needed, both ends are through-hole pads):\n  CT = Net-(J2-Pad2): J2-2 south to between C1 and C2, west to L1-2. 4 mm wide.\n  GATE_Q1: Q1-G to R3-2. 0.5 mm, about 12 mm long."
		(at 174 63 0)
